# 7. Right-align text. Pement: sed -e :a -e 's/^.\{1,78\}$/ &/;ta'
# A loop. :a is a label. The s adds one space in front of any line shorter
# than 79 characters (& is the whole match); t branches back to a if that
# substitution succeeded. The loop ends when the line is 79 wide. The width
# here is 18 so it fits the pane: \{1,17\} is "one to seventeen characters".
# Try: centre instead with  s/^.\{1,17\}$/ & /  (a space on both sides).
:a
s/^.\{1,17\}$/ &/;ta

